values ('5d287952-9301-4c55-a6ce-3f01c0000de3', '4efdcd38-f5e6-4f15-ac4f-76d8788c8053', 'debugging-and-errors', 'Debugging and reading errors', 'Use tracebacks, small experiments, and boundary tests to find the real cause of a bug.', 'intermediate', 40, 8, '["Read a traceback from the last line upward","Distinguish a symptom from its cause","Test boundary cases such as empty input and zero","Fix a bug without breaking existing behavior"]'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Debugging is a controlled investigation. Read the error, locate the failing line, form one hypothesis, and test it. Guessing repeatedly without evidence usually adds bugs.","sections":[{"title":"Read the traceback","paragraphs":["Tracebacks read from the bottom up: the final line names the exception, and the frame above it shows the line that raised it. The first useful clue is often the exception type.","`TypeError` usually means a value has the wrong type. `NameError` means a name was used before assignment. `IndexError` means an index is outside the sequence."],"code":"def double(value):\n    return value * 2\n\ndouble(\"3\")  # ''33'' — valid Python, likely the wrong intent\ndouble([1])  # [1, 1]\n"},{"title":"Test the boundaries","paragraphs":["Bugs often hide at the edges: empty lists, zero, one item, negative values, and missing keys. Write the smallest input that reproduces the problem."],"code":"def average(values):\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n\n# average([]) raises ZeroDivisionError"},{"title":"Fix the cause","paragraphs":["If the error is division by zero, decide what the function should mean for an empty list. Returning a default, raising a clear error, or requiring non-empty input are all valid—but the choice must be deliberate."],"code":"def average(values):\n    if not values:\n        return None\n    return sum(values) / len(values)"}],"keyPoints":["Start from the exception type and the line that raised it.","Reproduce with the smallest input.","Check boundaries before adding broad try/except blocks.","Fix the cause, not the visible symptom."]}'::jsonb, true)
